From 100d7043a6dd7444384b9d5c6a6198152e142b48 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pirates-killer <5260852+pirates-killer@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 03:46:25 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] goodixmilanf: Add driver for Goodix Milan F (27c6:5301)

The Goodix 27c6:5301 reader (GF5288-family sensor, chip ID 0x2202,
108x88 px, behind an HT32 MCU running "HT_APP" firmware) ships in
laptops such as the Dell Inspiron 5575. It enumerates as a CDC-ACM
device and speaks the Goodix message-pack protocol without TLS.

The protocol, sensor config, OTP calibration and frame descrambling
(16-bit LFSR XOR stream + CRC32/MPEG-2) were reverse engineered from the
Goodix Windows driver milanFusb.dll 1.0.33.600 for interoperability and
verified against the device.

The sensor is too small for NBIS/bozorth3 (0-2 minutiae per image), so
the driver is an FpDevice that matches on the host with SIGFM (SIFT +
geometric consistency, based on the goodix-fp-linux-dev implementation)
and stores the enrolled samples in a raw print. Finger detection polls
frames against an adaptive baseline that repairs itself if it was taken
with a finger on the sensor. Requires OpenCV.
